  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the given circuit the current through battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> just after closing the switch &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&#39; will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0059_133c0c232e82.png\" style=\"width: 229px; height: 150px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Just after closing the switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, inductor behaves like an open circuit, so no current will flow through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistors.</p><p>Thus, current through the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;(Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistors are in series).</p></blockquote>"
  }
}